1. Scope and definitions

"Licensor" means each copyright holder offering their own material under
this License. "You" means the person or organization exercising the rights
granted here. "Covered Material" means the original NameFirst code,
documentation, build files, and other copyrightable material offered under
this License, including subsequent modifications to that material.

Upstream uBlacklist material, imported upstream rules, third-party packages,
and other separately licensed material are NOT Covered Material. Their own
licenses continue to apply. In a modified upstream file, this License covers
only the original NameFirst additions or modifications offered under it;
it does not replace the license of the pre-existing material. Consult
LICENSE_SCOPE.md, NOTICE, UPSTREAM.json, and the accompanying third-party
notices to identify these boundaries. No exclusive right over names, facts,
public website addresses, or other uncopyrightable information is asserted.

"Modified Version" means Covered Material that You have changed or a work
incorporating or derived from Covered Material. Independently created works
merely distributed alongside it are not Covered Material.

"Distribution" means providing copies of Covered Material or a Modified
Version to another person or organization, whether as source, a compiled
extension, another executable, or any other form. Private use and internal
sharing within the same organization are not Distribution under this License.
Operating a network service without providing copies is not Distribution;
the restrictions on Commercial Exploitation still apply to that service.

2. Permission

Subject to these conditions, each Licensor grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, study,
modify, and distribute their Covered Material for Permitted Use.

"Permitted Use" includes personal use, learning, research, unpaid community
projects, free distribution, and an organization's internal use without
selling, charging for, or otherwise monetizing the Covered Material or its
functionality. This includes free internal use by a for-profit organization
and use by its employees in their ordinary work.

3. No Commercial Exploitation

You must not commercially exploit Covered Material or a Modified Version
without a separate written permission from every relevant rights holder.
"Commercial Exploitation" includes:

(a) selling, renting, or licensing access to the material or its functionality
    for a fee, subscription, mandatory donation, or other consideration;
(b) offering paid hosted services or paid support, installation, customization,
    or consulting whose subject is the material or a Modified Version;
(c) monetizing its distribution, interface, results, or operation through
    advertising, sponsorship, affiliate commissions, sale of user data, or
    similar revenue arrangements; and
(d) bundling the material into a paid or otherwise monetized product or service,
    including disguising a charge as a fee for another bundled component.

Free internal business use allowed by section 2 is not Commercial
Exploitation merely because it helps an organization conduct its business.
Visiting commercial websites, purchasing unrelated goods, or doing unrelated
paid work with ordinary search assistance is not prohibited. General hosting
platform advertisements outside the distributed project's interface do not
by themselves turn a free public source repository into Commercial
Exploitation, provided You receive no revenue from those advertisements.

4. Distribution and public corresponding source

Whenever You distribute Covered Material or a Modified Version, You must:

(a) provide a copy of this License, retain applicable copyright, attribution,
    and license notices, and identify Your material changes and their dates;
(b) license the Covered Material and Your modifications to it under this same
    License, version 1.0, without additional restrictions on its permitted use;
(c) make the complete Corresponding Source for the exact distributed version
    publicly available, without payment or a required account, at the time of
    Distribution, and provide recipients with a clear source download address
    or include it with the distributed source; and
(d) keep that source available for as long as You offer the distributed version
    and for at least three years after Your last Distribution of that version.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred editable form of the distributed
Covered Material and all Your modifications, together with the scripts,
configuration, dependency manifests, lockfiles, and instructions needed to
build and install the distributed version. Minified, obfuscated, generated,
or compiled files alone do not satisfy this requirement.

For separately licensed components needed to build the version, include
their source where their license requires it; otherwise provide exact
versions and publicly accessible retrieval instructions or sources. General
purpose tools that are not part of the distributed software need not be
included. Do not publish private signing keys, credentials, or personal user
data; provide safe configuration instructions or example values instead.

Distribution of an unchanged copy also requires identifying its exact
Corresponding Source. An existing public source location may be used, but
You remain responsible for meeting this section if it becomes unavailable.

Private modifications need not be published until Distribution occurs.
These reciprocal requirements apply only to Covered Material and changes
to it. They do not relicense upstream or third-party material, impose this
License on independent works, or remove rights already granted by another
license. Recipients receive the permissions here directly from the relevant
Licensors, subject to these same conditions.

